    "source": "1790 census projected to 1792, free adult men outside the Southern states; the 1790 census gives only free white males 16 and over, so men 21+ are estimated. Voters were men meeting each state's rules: most states required a freehold, property or taxpaying qualification (Vermont and Kentucky did not). Electors were chosen by popular vote in 6 states; elsewhere (Connecticut, Delaware, Georgia, New Jersey, New York, North Carolina, Rhode Island, South Carolina and Vermont) men cast no presidential vote. Free Black men could vote in some Northern states on the same or stricter terms."
   },
   {
    "key": "women",
    "label": "Women outside the South",
    "adults": 0.55,
    "barred": 0.951,
    "home": 0.049,
